/00-246C-0000-0023-8C45-9',0,1014,29,NULL,NULL,1,NULL,NULL),(144,NULL,NULL,'http://hdl.handle.net/11022/1009-0000-0007-0700-1@format=cmdi',0,1014,30,NULL,NULL,1,NULL,NULL),(145,NULL,'FOLK_E_00069','http://hdl.handle.net/10932/00-0332-C1F1-E9F4-4201-5',0,1015,0,NULL,NULL,1,NULL,NULL),(146,NULL,'FOLK_E_00070','http://hdl.handle.net/10932/00-0332-C1F6-A274-5201-4',0,1015,1,NULL,NULL,1,NULL,NULL),(147,NULL,NULL,'http://aa',1,1016,0,NULL,NULL,1,NULL,NULL),(148,NULL,NULL,'http://bb',1,1016,1,NULL,NULL,1,NULL,NULL),(149,'In Italian, grazie - thanks and ringraziare - to thank historically introduce an object by means of the preposition di- of(Renzi et al 1991: 545-548); when grazie and ringraziare introduce a subordinate infinite clause, they may all the same be followed by either di or per -for, the latter being the habitual preposition introducing an implicit causal subordinate (Renzi et al ibid.). In light of these considerations, a general lower frequency of occurrence of collocations with per would be expected. This article argues that, in contemporary Italian, there has been an increase in the use of constructions with per and that such an increase would be due to an influence from the English thanks/to thank for. Through diachronic lexicographic, quantitative and qualitative analyses carried out over a range of dictionaries and corpora, the results will show that from 1200 to 2011, the frequency of use of forms with per has indeed more than octupled in writing and that, from 1965 to 2003, it has more than doubled in speech. Moreover, by analysing the distribution of the studied constructions in a corpus of dubbed Italian from (American) English, the article will also explore the possibility that language contact with English, mainly via dubbing translations, may have played a concurrent fundamental role for such changes','A corpus-based investigation of language change in Italian: The case of grazie/ringraziare di and grazie/ringraziare per','doi:10.1075/jhl.16022.vio',1,1017,0,NULL,NULL,1,NULL,NULL),(150,'This document contains all the corpus metadata, including alternative links to the film scripts in both languages, information on the films, etc.','DuFLOR metadata document','https://1drv.ms/x/s!AvUE_P8AacsOgP4Wo5n5U9tVWxWkqQ',0,1017,1,NULL,NULL,1,NULL,NULL),(151,'Please notice that this is not a permalink','Mary Poppins (1964) - Original script','http://www.actorpoint.com/movie-scripts/scripts/mary-poppins.html',1,1017,2,NULL,NULL,1,NULL,NULL),(152,'Please notice that this is not a permalink','Mary Poppins (1964) - Italian version','http://www.oocities.org/anjaqantina/marypoppins.html',1,1017,3,NULL,NULL,1,NULL,NULL),(153,'Please notice that this is not a permalink','Dr Strangelove (1964) - Original script','http://www.visual-memory.co.uk/amk/doc/0055.html',1,1017,4,NULL,NULL,1,NULL,NULL),(154,'Please notice that this is not a permalink','Il Dottor Stranamore (1964) - Italian version','http://www.oocities.org/anjaqantina/stranamore.html',1,1017,5,NULL,NULL,1,NULL,NULL),(155,'Please notice that this is not a permalink','A Space Odyssey (1968) - Original script','http://miscel.wikidot.com/2001-transcript',1,1017,6,NULL,NULL,1,NULL,NULL),(156,'Please notice that this is not a permalink','2001: Odissea nello Spazio (1968) - Italian version','http://www.oocities.org/anjaqantina/2001.html',1,1017,7,NULL,NULL,1,NULL,NULL),(157,'Please notice that this is not a permalink','The Andromeda Strain (1971) - English script','https://www.springfieldspringfield.co.uk/movie_script.php?movie=andromeda-strain-the',1,1017,8,NULL,NULL,1,NULL,NULL),(158,'Please notice that this is not a permalink','Andromeda (1971) - Italian version','http://www.oocities.org/anjaqantina/andromeda.html',1,1017,9,NULL,NULL,1,NULL,NULL),(159,'Please notice that this is not a permalink','The Young Frankenstein (1974) - English script','http://www.angelfire.com/my/siteofkoolstuph/gw_youngfrankenstein_transcript.html',1,1017,10,NULL,NULL,1,NULL,NULL),(160,'Please notic